  "lesson": {
    "instructions": "Use your thumb (p) for the thick low E string, always open (fret 0). Use your index or middle finger for the thin high E melody at frets 4, 2 and 0.\n\nAfter the count-in, bars 3-4 practise bass alone: play for two beats, then rest for two. Bars 5-8 alternate a bass bar with the 4-2-0 phrase. Bars 9-18 play a bass bar, then the whole four-bar tune; repeat once.\n\nPlay bass first, then melody. No two notes together yet. Start at 50 BPM and slow down whenever you need.",
